---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About | All Systems Go!"
  closingTitle="Want to talk it through?"
  closingText="Tell us what you are facing and we will say honestly whether we can help."
>
  <section class="hero simple">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="label accent">About</span>
      <h1>Strategy for people who have to act on it</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap about-grid">
      <img class="portrait" src="/images/dan.jpg" alt="Dan Palmer" width="800" height="1000" style="width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover">
      <div style="display:grid;gap:28px">
        <div class="prose" style="font-size:19px;color:var(--fg)">
          <p>Dan Palmer has been consulting since 2017 and running his own consultancies since 2019, most recently All Systems Go!</p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted)">He holds an MBA from the University of Amsterdam, focused on strategy and innovation management. Before consulting he worked in financial markets, from derivatives trading to content recognition systems, and then moved into product management and business design.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted)">The work today spans strategy, roadmapping, and the design of new products and businesses, for clients from Microsoft and Samsung to Asana and Wärtsilä.</p>
                    <p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danieljpalmer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent)">Dan on LinkedIn &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="label">Job titles on the record</span>
          <div class="titles" style="margin-top:12px">
            <span class="tag">Strategy Philosopher</span><span class="tag">Innovation Cartographer</span><span class="tag">Customer Experience Composer</span><span class="tag">Schrödinger's Strategist</span><span class="tag">Agent Provocateur</span>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:14px">Once called a strategy anarchist, which was meant as a compliment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>